WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.313
Secure subprocess usage in Python means launching external programs only
when necessary and doing so with explicit trust boundaries.

2
00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:22.709
The application should know which executable will run, which arguments are
data, whether a shell is involved, which directory is used, which files
are accessible, which environment values are passed, which identity is
used, how long the process may run, and how output will be handled.

3
00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:31.049
Strong designs avoid shell interpretation, separate executables from
structured arguments, and map user choices to allowlisted internal
operations.

4
00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:44.648
They validate inputs, constrain paths and working directories, minimize
inherited environment state, protect secrets, control standard input and
output, apply least privilege, set timeouts, and translate errors into
safe user-facing behavior.

5
00:00:44.648 --> 00:00:48.369
Each control reduces ambiguity around what the child process can do.

6
00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:56.901
Subprocess security connects to file handling, secrets management,
authorization, safe logging, deployment design, monitoring, and incident
response.

7
00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.275
A subprocess call is not just a utility line.

8
00:00:59.275 --> 00:01:04.920
It can reach across application boundaries into the operating system and
surrounding infrastructure.

9
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:11.976
That is why review should include successful execution, rejected inputs,
failure modes, output handling, and cleanup behavior.

10
00:01:11.976 --> 00:01:22.048
The practical goal is predictable, reviewable, least-privilege process
execution that supports business needs without turning Python applications
into unsafe command interfaces.

11
00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.780
Prefer libraries when they fit.

12
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.527
When subprocess is necessary, keep the code explicit, narrow, observable,
and tested.

13
00:01:28.527 --> 00:01:32.440
That discipline makes automation safer and easier to operate over time.
